    {
      "id": "co-04-conditionnel-passe",
      "title": "Step 4: I would have: the conditionnel passé",
      "fr": "le conditionnel passé",
      "level": "B1",
      "keywords": [
        "step by step",
        "conditionnel passé",
        "would have",
        "j'aurais",
        "je serais venu",
        "j'aurais dû",
        "regret"
      ],
      "topics": [],
      "see": [
        "conditionnel-passe",
        "passe-compose-etre"
      ],
      "tense": "conditionnel-passe",
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "In short",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "*J'aurais fait* = I would have done. It is the **conditional of avoir or être** + the **past participle**, with the same auxiliary as in the passé composé. It talks about a past that did not happen, and about regrets: *J'aurais dû travailler.*"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "verb": "faire",
              "tense": "conditionnel-passe"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Avoir or être",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "Verbs that take *être* in the passé composé (*aller, venir, partir, rester, arriver, tomber* and reflexive verbs) take it here too, and the participle agrees with the subject: *elle serait venue, nous serions restés*."
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "verb": "venir",
              "tense": "conditionnel-passe"
            },
            {
              "type": "check",
              "item": {
                "type": "form",
                "verb": "aller",
                "tense": "conditionnel-passe",
                "person": 0
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Regrets and reproaches",
          "blocks": [
