    {
      "id": "co-06-mix",
      "title": "Step 6: The three si-sentences mixed",
      "fr": "les trois types de phrases avec si",
      "level": "A2",
      "levelTo": "B1",
      "keywords": [
        "step by step",
        "si",
        "if",
        "mix",
        "real condition",
        "si + présent",
        "si + imparfait",
        "si + plus-que-parfait"
      ],
      "topics": [],
      "see": [
        "si-clauses"
      ],
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "In short",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "There are three kinds of *si* sentence, chosen by how real the situation is. **Real:** si + présent → présent or futur. **Imagined now:** si + imparfait → conditionnel. **Imagined past:** si + plus-que-parfait → conditionnel passé."
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "head": [
                "kind",
                "si part",
                "other part",
                "example",
                "English"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "real",
                  "présent",
                  "présent / futur",
                  "S'il pleut, je resterai.",
                  "If it rains, I'll stay."
                ],
                [
                  "imagined now",
                  "imparfait",
                  "conditionnel",
                  "S'il pleuvait, je resterais.",
                  "If it rained, I'd stay."
                ],
                [
                  "imagined past",
                  "plus-que-parfait",
                  "conditionnel passé",
                  "S'il avait plu, je serais resté.",
                  "If it had rained, I'd have stayed."
                ]
              ],
              "textCols": [
                0,
                1,
                2,
                4
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "How to choose",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "Ask: **can it still happen?** Yes → real (*si + présent*). **Is it untrue now?** → imagined now. **Did it not happen?** → imagined past."
            },
            {
              "type": "tip",
              "en": "Czech uses the future in a real condition about tomorrow. French uses the **present** after *si*: *s'il pleut demain*, never *s'il pleuvra*.",
              "title": "Different from Czech"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Examples",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "examples",
              "items": [
                {
                  "fr": "Si tu as faim, prends une pomme.",
                  "en": "If you're hungry, take an apple."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Si j'avais un chien, je le promènerais tous les jours.",
                  "en": "If I had a dog, I'd walk it every day."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Si j'avais su, je ne serais pas venu.",
                  "en": "If I had known, I wouldn't have come."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "S'il fait beau demain, on ira à la plage.",
                  "en": "If it's nice tomorrow, we'll go to the beach."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
